<%/* ---- Glossary ---- */%>
<div class="content-card">
    <h2 id="glossary" style="font-size: 18px; margin: 0 0 8px;">Glossary</h2>
    <dl class="row mb-0 small">
        <dt class="col-sm-3">ArchivesSpace (AS)</dt>
        <dd class="col-sm-9">The descriptive metadata system. Resources + archival objects describe what a package <em>is</em>.</dd>
        <dt class="col-sm-3">Archivematica (AM)</dt>
        <dd class="col-sm-9">The preservation-processing system that turns a submission into a standards-based archival package.</dd>
        <dt class="col-sm-3">SIP</dt>
        <dd class="col-sm-9">Submission Information Package — what Archivematica ingests.</dd>
        <dt class="col-sm-3">AIP</dt>
        <dd class="col-sm-9">Archival Information Package — the preserved output stored long-term.</dd>
        <dt class="col-sm-3">DuraCloud</dt>
        <dd class="col-sm-9">Archivematica's storage layer the worker waits on during ingest.</dd>
        <dt class="col-sm-3">Wasabi&nbsp;S3</dt>
        <dd class="col-sm-9">The S3 preservation tier where AIPs are copied for long-term storage.</dd>
        <dt class="col-sm-3">Handle / PID</dt>
        <dd class="col-sm-9">The persistent identifier minted for each object (the <code>hdl.handle.net</code> link) / its internal id.</dd>
        <dt class="col-sm-3"><code>uri.txt</code></dt>
        <dd class="col-sm-9">A sidecar file linking a package to its ArchivesSpace digital-object URI.</dd>
        <dt class="col-sm-3">Collection</dt>
        <dd class="col-sm-9">A repository record bound to an ArchivesSpace resource; objects belong to one.</dd>
        <dt class="col-sm-3">Elasticsearch</dt>
        <dd class="col-sm-9">The search index that powers staff search and public discovery.</dd>
        <dt class="col-sm-3">Kaltura</dt>
        <dd class="col-sm-9">The streaming platform for audio/video derivatives.</dd>
    </dl>
</div>
